# solari-doctor — scoped ignore rules.
# The cookbook's root .gitignore already covers node_modules/, .env, .venv/.
# These add what this project needs on top of it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Research / verification material — LOCAL ONLY, never pushed.
#
# Everything below was produced while verifying the SDK's real behaviour before
# any code was written. It is the evidence trail, not the deliverable. From
# here on, only what we actually build ships to GitHub.
#
# Reverse any single line here if a document should join the submission.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/docs
CLAUDE.md
/scripts
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Credentials — SOLARI_API_KEY must never be committed.
# Defensive: the cookbook root already ignores `.env`, restated here so the
# rule survives if this directory is ever extracted on its own.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies (restated for the same reason)
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test / tooling output
coverage/
.nyc_output/
.vitest/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# The cookbook root ignores `package-lock.json` for its examples, which are
# meant to be copied and run loosely. solari-doctor is a tool, not an example:
# it pins exact versions (see .npmrc `save-exact=true`) and its lockfile is
# part of the deliverable. Re-include it for this subtree only.
!package-lock.json
